l do here in just a minute it's  going to put an alpha channel on here I  don't want the Alpha Channel it's also  going to use the animation codec which  is high quality codec but it's a very  large file size again so you can pick  anything here h.264 photo JPEG I  typically like to work with pro res file  so I'm gonna use a four to two codec  click OK  audio output is set to auto there is no  audio so I'll I can leave it on auto or  I'll let's go ahead and turn it off I'll  click OK and then I'm going to tell  After Effects where to save this file  which I've already got set up in a  folder here called proxies and I'll just  leave it the same name and at this point  all I have to do is click render and  it's going to create the proxy file  okay so it just finished rendering and  if you look back up in the project  window you can see on the original  footage there's now a gray box right  here which means hey this footage is now  a proxy you can also see that the file  size went from nine hundred and some-odd  megabytes to two hundred and  seventy-five megabytes so now we're  working with a much smaller file size  and it's automatically updated in our  project window I'm actually gonna go  ahead and delete this second composition  that After Effects made for rendering  purposes so there you go so we have a  proxy file in here and if i zoom in 200%  if you look at the edges here you can  tell it's a little bit lower res when I  click this gray box this is the cool  part is it will automatically go back to  the original footage instead of the  proxy and you'll see on the edges here  watch the difference on the edging  that's full res proxy full res proxy I  don't know how much of that you can  actually see in the compression on the  web here but it's a noticeable  difference and also you'll notice when I  click off the proxy the file size goes  right back to 960 a because that's the  original so proxy 275 original nine 68  and that's pretty much all you have to  do you can work with the footage down  here when you're ready to render you can  just shut off the proxy go to render  like you'd normally would and render out  a high risk file so there you go there's  the basics of working with proxies  inside After Effects there are a few  more things you can dive into with  proxies I'm not going to get into those  today in this video but that gives you  the essence of proxies and how to speed  up your After Effects workflow I hope  that you learned something new today and  I would love if you would like or  comment below and let me know what you  thought until next time  I'm Cameron and this is motion science
 

